    "text": "Done! I've successfully implemented a bounded stack in Cuis with all required functionality:\n\n**BoundedStack class** (`'BoundedStack'` category):\n- `push:` \u2014 adds an object (raises \"stack is full\" if at capacity)\n- `pop` \u2014 removes and returns the top object (raises \"stack is empty\" if empty)\n- `top` \u2014 returns top without removing (raises \"stack is empty\" if empty)\n- `isEmpty` \u2014 returns true if no elements\n- `size` \u2014 returns current element count\n- `withCapacity:` \u2014 class method to create a stack with validation (raises \"capacity must be a positive integer\" if invalid)\n\n**BoundedStackTest class** (`'BoundedStack-Tests'` category):\n14 comprehensive tests covering all behaviors:\n- Valid creation and initialization\n- Invalid capacity validation (non-positive, non-integer values)\n- Push/pop operations and LIFO behavior\n- Size tracking\n- Error messages for full/empty stack operations\n- Multiple operations in sequence\n\nAll 14 tests pass. The image has been saved and is ready for review."
